# SCPI instrument server (ww-otj.77): server.xml serves five tags on 127.0.0.1:5025. Bennu has no SCPI, so there is no stock oracle and
# DUT defaults to rust. The peers are PyVISA + pyvisa-py and lxi-tools (independent clients), our own `ferrofire scpi` (PEER_BIN, the same
# binary as the device), and python sockets for the churn / overlong / garbage cases; a stand-in provider (provider.py) answers the writes.
CFG=${CFG:-${here:-/conformance}/${proto:-scpi}/server.xml}
DUT_DEFAULT=rust
WARMUP=3
CAPTURE_FILTER='tcp port 5025 or tcp port 4880 or tcp port 111 or tcp port 4881 or udp port 111'
# The raw socket is plain TCP text: no dissector, so the checks assert on TCP and on the transcript (check.sh). HiSLIP (4880) and VXI-11
# (portmapper 111, core 4881) have Wireshark dissectors, whose malformed and expert rows judge the framing and the RPC/XDR independently.
PROTO_FILTER='tcp.port == 5025 || tcp.port == 4880 || tcp.port == 111 || tcp.port == 4881 || udp.port == 111'
# 2000 short connections end in resets and half-closes, and the 200 KB overlong line is sent faster than the device reads it, so the
# window closes for a moment: the TCP analyzer calls those Warn, and they are flow control working, not malformed traffic
EXPERT_ALLOW='Connection reset|Connection finish|window specified by the receiver is now completely full|Zero Window'
PEER_BIN=target-linux/debug/ferrofire
# peer.sh counts the device's open descriptors in /proc/<pid>/fd, so the peers container needs its process namespace
PEER_FLAGS='--pid container:ff-conf-dut --cap-add SYS_PTRACE'
# Zeek has no SCPI analyzer; conn.log (built in) still records every connection
ZEEK_LOAD=''
ZEEK_REQUIRED=${ZEEK_REQUIRED:-1}
